      "question": "Where does money flow into marketing spend and which downstream slice from Sales & Marketing appears as the dominant line item?",
      "question_style": "natural_language",
      "ground_truth": {
        "task_type": "vague_multi",
        "answer": {
          "type": "open_ended",
          "value": "Series A cash feeds the operating pool (about 8k in the graph), and the operating pool pushes a much larger 12.3k chunk straight into Sales & Marketing—so that trunk is the main artery into GTM. Once you land inside Sales & Marketing, Paid Ads pulls the biggest single ribbon (roughly 3.7k) compared with events or tools, which matches the yellow highlight: acquisition channels—not back-office widgets—eat most of the marketing envelope."
        },
        "key_insights": [
          "Operating Fund → Sales & Marketing is the heavy bridge out of the Series A tranche.",
          "Within Sales & Marketing, Paid Ads outweighs the other outgoing splits."
